-- title:
--   One exponential envelope bounds every local-cover dimension
-- statement:
--   For any natural number $h$, put $L=512h$, $v=\binom{L}{h}$, and $M=2^{600000(h+1)^2}$. Let $p$ be the construction's selected local prime, $c=\lceil4(p+v)/p\rceil$ its bucket cap, $R=p^{2L}$ the candidate-row count, and $T=320(2h+1)(\lfloor\log_2(p^2)\rfloor+1)$ the schedule length. Then
--   $$\max\left\{1,L+1,v+1,p+1,c+1,R+1,T+1,p^{2L+1}+1,2^{L+1}+1\right\}\le M.$$
--
--   These simultaneous bounds cover the local-cover tables, schedule, candidate decoding, and mask arithmetic. They provide a single magnitude parameter for subsequent polynomial resource estimates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverMagnitude.lean#L69-L93

